      "html": "<p>A smaller cichlid from Honduras. Males reach a maximum length of 13 cm, while females always stay smaller.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cryptoheros_cutteri_en/",
      "html": "<p>Despite the comparatively small size, one should not keep these cichlids in small tanks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cryptoheros_cutteri_en/",
      "html": "<p>They have a very vivid temper, especially when they care for the offspring.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cryptoheros_cutteri_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species of Cryptoheros differ from the other members of the Central American Cichlasoma relationship inter alia by the fact that they prefer to spawn on places that are a bit hidden. So the fish display an intermediate behaviour between typical open spawners and cave spawners. Both parents take intensive care of eggs and juveniles.</p>"
